# Local Bazel overrides -- copy to `.bazelrc.user` (gitignored) and edit.
#
# `.bazelrc` try-imports `.bazelrc.user` last, so anything here wins over the
# committed config. The committed defaults already point at the lab Buildbarn
# cluster (grpc://bb.lab.wayvz.io:8980, reachable over Tailscale); use this
# file to change that per machine.
#
# Work fully offline by default (same as passing --config=local every time):
#
#   build --config=local
#
# Point at a different Buildbarn (e.g. a local podman cluster):
#
#   build --remote_executor=grpc://localhost:8980
#   build --remote_instance_name=hardlinking
#   build --bes_backend=
#
# NixOS: .bazelrc pins --shell_executable=/bin/bash for the remote workers and
# that path does not exist locally. The devshell hook (flake.nix) appends the
# override below automatically; outside the devshell add it by hand.
#
#   common:local --shell_executable=/run/current-system/sw/bin/bash
#
# The `remote_platform` exec_properties in //tools/remote-toolchains must match
# the queue the cluster's scheduler advertises, or actions queue with no worker.
